# BusyBox init reads this table top-to-bottom exactly once at boot.
# CRITICAL: at least one entry MUST be "respawn" - without it, init
# runs through the table, finds nothing left to do, and exits.
# PID 1 exiting is fatal to the kernel (see: our earlier panic).

# Run system initialization: mounts, module loading order, etc.
# "sysinit" actions run once, in order, before anything else.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# Respawn a session-launcher script forever on the main console.
# If the game (or the graphical session around it) crashes, this
# process exits, and init immediately restarts it - this IS our
# "supervisor" for the kiosk, achieved with nothing more than
# BusyBox init's respawn mechanism.
tty1::respawn:/usr/bin/osukiosk-session

# Handle Ctrl-Alt-Del gracefully instead of an immediate hard reset.
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# Ensure a clean unmount sequence on shutdown/reboot signals.
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r